From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 24 Jul 2026 12:05:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] iommu/arm-smmu-v3: demote benign FW-config notes to dev_dbg

On O6N (Radxa Orion, ACPI/IORT boot) the SMMUv3 probe emits three
dev_warn lines that are expected firmware-configuration notes, not
faults. At warn level they show up in `dmesg -l err,warn` and read as
errors, so demote them to dev_dbg. None of the surrounding logic changes.

1) arm_smmu_init_strtab_2lvl():

     arm-smmu-v3 ...: 2-level strtab only covers M/N bits of SID

   The L1 stream table is intentionally capped at STRTAB_MAX_L1_ENTRIES.
   When IDR1.SIDSIZE advertises more SID bits than the capped table
   covers, the driver notes it and proceeds -- SIDs the platform actually
   uses are within range on Sky1. Informational, expected.

2) arm_smmu_get_httu():

     arm-smmu-v3 ...: IDR0.HTTU features(0x..) overridden by FW configuration (0x..)

   On ACPI the IORT HTTU bits, not IDR0.HTTU, are authoritative. When the
   two differ the FW description wins by design; the comment above the call
   ("ACPI IORT sets the HTTU bits") documents this. Expected on Sky1.

3) arm_smmu_device_hw_probe(), coherency check:

     arm-smmu-v3 ...: IDR0.COHACC overridden by FW configuration (..)

   Same class: FW-declared coherency is used in preference to IDR0.COHACC,
   and the code already comments "used in preference to the ID register,
   but warn on mismatch". The mismatch is expected and harmless here.

All three are dev_warn benign-mismatch/cap notes (not dev_info, so they do
show under err,warn) and the fallback each describes is the correct, intended
behaviour. arm-smmu-v3 is an upstream core driver; the change is limited to
the three dev_warn->dev_dbg tokens for a clean -rc rebase.

Signed-off-by: Jason Perlow <jperlow@gmail.com>
Upstream-Status: Pending
---
--- a/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu-v3/arm-smmu-v3.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/arm/arm-smmu-v3/arm-smmu-v3.c
@@ -4452,7 +4452,7 @@
 	/* Calculate the L1 size, capped to the SIDSIZE. */
 	cfg->l2.num_l1_ents = min(last_sid_idx + 1, STRTAB_MAX_L1_ENTRIES);
 	if (cfg->l2.num_l1_ents <= last_sid_idx)
-		dev_warn(smmu->dev,
+		dev_dbg(smmu->dev,
 			 "2-level strtab only covers %u/%u bits of SID\n",
 			 ilog2(cfg->l2.num_l1_ents * STRTAB_NUM_L2_STES),
 			 smmu->sid_bits);
@@ -4954,7 +4954,7 @@
 		smmu->features |= hw_features;
 	else if (hw_features != fw_features)
 		/* ACPI IORT sets the HTTU bits */
-		dev_warn(smmu->dev,
+		dev_dbg(smmu->dev,
 			 "IDR0.HTTU features(0x%x) overridden by FW configuration (0x%x)\n",
 			  hw_features, fw_features);
 }
@@ -5026,7 +5026,7 @@
 	 * register, but warn on mismatch.
 	 */
 	if (!!(reg & IDR0_COHACC) != coherent)
-		dev_warn(smmu->dev, "IDR0.COHACC overridden by FW configuration (%s)\n",
+		dev_dbg(smmu->dev, "IDR0.COHACC overridden by FW configuration (%s)\n",
 			 str_true_false(coherent));
 
 	switch (FIELD_GET(IDR0_STALL_MODEL, reg)) {
